From b7d5be102a57ec8f3166a40f631b24010122d913 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Title screen: Press Start stays until the player presses
 START, the intro is not shown again

The intro movie plays once when the game starts; then the Press Start title waits for START with no time
limit. The original left the title after 600 frames (about 10 seconds) and played the intro again, over
and over.

src/main/main.c runLandingScreen: the frame counter and its limit are gone, the loop only ends with START.
The intro still plays at boot and after the ending, where the original also returns to it. main_BSS_END
-16 B.
---
 src/main/main.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main/main.c b/src/main/main.c
index 7532f12..ef900a8 100644
--- a/src/main/main.c
+++ b/src/main/main.c
@@ -3713,13 +3713,11 @@ void initializeFramebuffer(void)
 void runLandingScreen(void)
 {
 	int32_t done;
-	int32_t timer;
 #if VERSION_IS(JP_TRIAL) || VERSION_IS(JP_BOMBOM)
 	int32_t i;
 #endif
 
 	done = 0;
-	timer = 0x258;
 #if VERSION_IS(JP_TRIAL) || VERSION_IS(JP_BOMBOM)
 	SECRET_CODE = -1;
 #endif
@@ -3731,7 +3729,9 @@ void runLandingScreen(void)
 	FADE_OUT_CURRENT = 0;
 	fadeFromBlack(0x28);
 
-	while (--timer > 0) {
+	/* MOD (title stays): the original went back to the intro movie after 600 frames; the title now
+	   waits for START */
+	for (;;) {
 		pollInputMenu();
 
 #if VERSION_IS(JP_TRIAL) || VERSION_IS(JP_BOMBOM)
-- 
